---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import DocPage from "../components/DocPage.astro";
import { render, legal, byName } from "../lib/md";
import { site } from "../config";
// The texts are docs/legal/*.md in the plugin repo (the plugin shows the same ones): edit them there.
const md = `
## Disclaimer
${byName(legal, "disclaimer.md")}

## Firmware warning
${byName(legal, "firmware-warning.md")}

## Back to stock
${byName(legal, "back-to-stock.md")}

## Library terms
${byName(legal, "library-terms.md")}

Full terms: [TERMS.md in the library repo](https://github.com/${site.libraryRepo}/blob/main/TERMS.md).

## Licences
- **The plugin** and the tools: GPL-3.0. It comes with no warranty and no liability (GPL-3.0 sections 15 and 16).
- **Library items**: each has its own licence, shown on its page (the ones by FX Unleashed are CC-BY-4.0).
- **Car rev light data**: Lovely Car Data by Lovely Sim Racing and contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, downloaded by the plugin at runtime.
- **Built-in Mustang dash**: after the SimHub dash "LMGT3 Ford Mustang GT3" by Redadeg (lmu-dashboards.com), used with the author's permission.
- **This website**: built with Astro and three.js (MIT). Fonts: Chakra Petch, Inter, JetBrains Mono (SIL Open Font License), from Google Fonts.
- **Trademarks**: Simagic and FX Pro are trademarks of their owner, used only to say which hardware this works with. The FX Unleashed logo is our own. The wheel drawings are outlines of the real wheels, with their lights where they are on the product.

## Privacy
This site doesn't track you: no analytics, no cookies, no accounts. Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, and the library and changelog from GitHub, so those services see your IP address like any website you visit.

The library and "Install" buttons talk to the plugin on your own PC (127.0.0.1): nothing about your PC is sent anywhere. The plugin checks GitHub for updates and the library index, and downloads car light data (Lovely Car Data); it sends nothing about you.

## Rights holders
If something here uses your work without permission, open an issue on [GitHub](${site.contact}) or contact the maintainers there. Library items are taken down while it's looked at.
`;
const { html, toc } = render(md);
---
<Base title="Legal" description="Disclaimer, firmware warning, library terms, licences and privacy.">
  <DocPage html={html} toc={toc} eyebrow="Legal">
    <Fragment slot="before"><h1>Legal</h1><p class="lead">The short version: independent, free, no warranty, no tracking. The long version is below.</p></Fragment>
  </DocPage>
</Base>
